 ## How it works
 **Inputs and Outputs:**
-*   **Input:** A set of 3D Gaussian ellipsoids $\{G_i\}$, where each Gaussian $i$ is defined by a mean position $\mu_i$, a covariance matrix $\Sigma_i$ (or rotation $R_i$ and scale $S_i$), and a base color. For normal rendering, an additional attribute $n_i$ (the surface normal vector) is associated with each Gaussian.
-*   **Output:** A rendered image containing surface normal vectors (typically encoded as RGB values) and optionally a depth map.
+*   **Input:** A set of 3D Gaussian ellipsoids derived from meshes (e.g., Stanford 3D Scanning Repository models like Bunny, Dragon, Armadillo) [S1, unofficial]. For normal rendering, an additional attribute $n_i$ (the surface normal vector) is associated with each Gaussian [S1, unofficial][G].
+*   **Output:** A rendered image containing surface normal vectors encoded as RGB values, and optionally a depth map [S1, unofficial][G].
 
